    TEST-0001: test book()'s rules with a fake file system
    
    book() read and wrote data/bookings.json itself, so a test could only
    run against the real file: every booking a test made stayed there for
    the next test, and for the next person who ran yarn start.
    
    Same move as the coffee cart. bookings.ts declares FileSystem, the two
    calls book() makes, and book() and schedule() take one. Node's fs
    module already has that shape, so main.ts passes fs itself and nothing
    needed to wrap it.
    
    FakeFileSystem hands back whatever JSON a test gives it and remembers
    what was written. Each rule gets a test: the 2-hour limit, an overlap,
    back-to-back bookings, and a student's third booking of the day.

